WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:04.891
With six films released in the Conjuring franchise
so far and at least three more planned for

00:00:04.891 --> 00:00:07.410
the near future, how do all of these films
stack up?

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:11.040
Are all possessions created equally, or are
some spirits more pernicious than others?

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:16.540
While the first Conjuring film is often warmly
regarded by horror fans, Annabelle, the prequel

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:18.440
that followed in 2014, is not.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:22.960
Annabelle made a respectable $257 million
worldwide, but reactions to the film were

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:24.040
far from kind.

00:00:24.449 --> 00:00:28.640
This spin-off focuses on a couple welcoming
their first child while also being terrorized

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.740
by a possessed doll that seems intent on taking
the mother's soul.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:35.960
What sets Annabelle apart from other entries
in the Conjuring Universe is just how stale

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:37.840
and uneventful the overall film feels.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:42.060
Throughout most of the film, the haunted doll
hardly moves or really even bothers the couple

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:42.880
who owns her.

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:46.600
Outside of some shots of Annabelle looking
intimidating or being positioned ominously

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:50.860
in a room, there isn't really much to keep
audiences on the edge of their seats.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.300
"What do you want from me?

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.320
WHAT DO YOU WANT FROM ME?!"

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:02.480
The Curse of La Llorona follows a mother trying
to protect her children from the titular undead

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:02.940
spirit.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:06.110
The film wastes what could have been an interesting
look at an underrepresented piece of Hispanic

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:08.920
folklore by instead making it into a formulaic
ghost movie.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.160
The characters don't really have any interesting
personalities - particularly the children,

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:17.410
who function more as props to drive the plot
than as actual human beings.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:21.550
Motherhood and conventional ideas about protecting
children are highlighted extensively, but

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:24.000
there's ultimately no commentary about those
themes.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.670
In the end, the film says nothing meaningful
and only manages to deliver a few cheap jump-scares

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:31.060
before the spirit is defeated and the film
ends.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:36.070
With its gothic set design and period costumes,
The Nun might be the most visually interesting

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:37.180
entry in the franchise.

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:41.060
However, a nicely constructed set and some
interesting costumes aren't enough to make

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:44.460
a film function, and it's safe to say viewers
weren't impressed overall.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:48.820
The film follows a novitiate who is determined
to find the root of the evil now emanating

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:52.320
from the monastery and banish a spirit that
has taken the form of an undead nun.

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:57.240
The Nun is packed with a handful of boring,
one-note characters, plenty of lazy dialogue,

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:59.910
and a deluge of forgettable jump scares.

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:04.390
Ultimately, The Nun manages to feel completely
flat and devoid of creative substance, despite

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.820
having some stylistic flare.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:10.400
Annabelle Comes Home serves as another prequel
to the the first Conjuring film.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:14.510
After Ed and Lorraine Warren come into possession
of the cursed Annabelle doll, the couple safely

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:16.800
confines the possessed plaything away from
the world.

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:19.920
Of course, one slip up is all it takes for
Annabelle to cause havoc.

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:24.300
When a girl wanders into the Warrens' locked
artifact room and accidentally releases Annabelle,

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.420
chaos reigns.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:30.140
Now free to terrorize as she pleases, Annabelle
releases a slew of angry spirits from the

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:34.469
couple's collection of cursed objects, turning
the once peaceful Warren home into a demonic

00:02:34.469 --> 00:02:35.240
house of horrors.

00:02:35.629 --> 00:02:39.640
While Annabelle Comes Home isn't the worst
film in the Conjuring universe, it is definitely

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:40.620
one of the most boring.

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:44.610
With a few exceptions, the demons aren't noteworthy
enough to make them stand out from the more

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:47.800
interesting cast of unholy spirits we've seen
in previous films.

00:02:48.609 --> 00:02:52.260
The Conjuring 2 is one of the best received
entries in the Conjuring series, but it still

00:02:52.269 --> 00:02:56.109
feels a little like the creative team tried
and failed to recapture lightning in a bottle

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:56.960
with this sequel.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:01.090
Like the first movie, The Conjuring 2 follows
Ed and Lorraine Warren as they work to save

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:02.940
a family from the demon that's tormenting
them.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:07.750
The film feels like it was made with the intention
of setting up an expanded universe instead

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:09.760
of telling a complete, self-contained story.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:14.460
Aside from the crowded roster of spirits,
the primary demon gives its name to Lorraine

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:17.880
in the beginning of the movie, which is the
key to defeating it in the end, making the

00:03:17.889 --> 00:03:19.709
resolution feel rushed and unearned.

00:03:19.709 --> 00:03:21.720
"I do know your name.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:22.920
I asked you.”

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.930
“TELL ME WHO YOU ARE!”

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:25.920
“And you told me!”

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:30.370
Despite these gripes, The Conjuring 2 is still
a worthy successor to the first film, making

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:35.219
use of interesting camera work, a slow build-up,
and the creepy imagery that fans of the franchise

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:35.820
have come to expect.

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:41.380
Featuring a cast of likable characters, lots
of creepy build-up, and tense pacing, Annabelle:

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:45.639
Creation reaffirms that the Conjuring series
can still deliver the paranormal frights that

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:46.180
horror fans crave.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:50.720
As a prequel to the first Annabelle film,
Annabelle: Creation shows the origin of the

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:51.700
demonic Annabelle doll.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:56.120
The film features competent acting from the
cast of child actors and decent writing to

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:56.980
support them as well.

00:03:57.389 --> 00:04:01.240
Though some of the scares end up falling flat,
there are some genuinely visceral moments

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:03.540
that help drive home the sadistic nature of
the demon.

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:08.040
There is a unique balance in Annabelle: Creation
between highlighting the emotional punishment

00:04:08.049 --> 00:04:12.209
endured by the possessed and the physical
punishment doled out by the sadistic spirit,

00:04:12.209 --> 00:04:15.960
letting the two complement each other and
build in anxiety-inducing ways.

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:19.140
The first entry in the franchise is also the
best.

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:23.360
Because there was no pre-existing, familiar
film universe for audiences, The Conjuring

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:25.130
had to be particularly paced.

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:28.700
Instead of being thrown into the paranormal
with little explanation, the characters are

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:33.200
forced to do research, set up and monitor
equipment, and work with local police just

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:35.140
to get enough proof to have an exorcism approved.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.940
As a result of all the added legwork, not
only does The Conjuring feel more believable

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:42.320
and accessible for audiences, but the frightening
pay-offs feel earned.

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.860
The chief marker of this film's quality is
the building of atmosphere.

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:49.780
This is demonstrated particularly well through
how reserved and understated some of the scares

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:50.780
are in the film.

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:55.100
The musical score is allowed to be soft and
to serve as a background to scares, instead

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:58.920
of the blaring, bass-heavy blasts that punctuate
jump cues in later movies.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:04.020
Additionally, the minimal CGI used throughout
the film is also done with precision, demonstrating

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:05.620
that less really is more.

